**School-Wide Vendor Governance Findings**

These findings relate to the policies, processes, and ownership structures that govern the school's vendor portfolio as a whole — not any individual vendor. They are drawn from Section VR2 (School-Wide Vendor Governance).

| **[HIGH]  ****Offboarding does not cover vendor account ownership** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 30 days  ·  Medium (3 days)  ·  HR / IT Director* When a staff member leaves, there is no process to transfer or revoke vendor account ownership. Vendor portal logins, billing contacts, and contract records may leave with the departing person, creating access gaps and continuity risk. **→ ***Add vendor account transfer to the IT offboarding checklist. For each departing staff member who owned vendor accounts, reassign those accounts before their last day. Check billing contacts and support portal accounts specifically — these are the most commonly overlooked.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****Software approval is informal — not consistently followed** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director* IT is usually consulted before new tools are adopted, but the process is informal and not required. Informal processes have gaps — particularly when new staff join who do not know the convention. **→ ***Formalise the approval process with a one-page policy and a simple request form. Make it a requirement, not a suggestion, for any tool that holds school or student data.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****No IT procurement spend threshold — shadow IT risk** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director / Head of School* There is no defined spend threshold below which IT or departments must obtain review before adopting a new tool. Without a threshold policy, staff can subscribe to tools that hold student data, auto-renew indefinitely, or create security gaps — all without IT or finance visibility. This is one of the most common sources of shadow IT in schools. **→ ***Define a simple spend threshold policy: for example, any subscription above $500/year or any tool that holds student or staff data requires IT review before adoption. A one-page policy shared with staff closes the most common gap. Pair it with the software approval process.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****IT and Business Office maintain separate vendor lists** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office* IT and the Business Office each maintain their own vendor list with no shared view. This creates duplicate effort and gaps — IT may not know about finance tools, and the Business Office may not know about IT-managed subscriptions. **→ ***Merge the two lists using this register as the foundation. Assign a shared owner and agree on a single source of truth going forward.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****Password manager used for some vendor accounts but not all** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director* Some vendor admin credentials are in a shared password manager, but not all. The accounts not covered represent single-person dependencies. **→ ***Audit which vendor accounts are not in the password manager and migrate them. Prioritise accounts for vendors that hold student or financial data.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****DPA tracking incomplete — not all student-data vendors covered** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director* A DPA register exists but does not cover all vendors that hold student data. Gaps in DPA coverage leave the school partially exposed. **→ ***Use this module's student-data findings to identify uncovered vendors. Request DPAs from any vendor holding student data that is not yet covered.* |
| --- |

| **[MEDIUM]  ****No annual vendor review process** *Vendor Governance  ·  Do within 90 days  ·  Short (1 day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office* The school does not conduct a deliberate annual pass through its vendor portfolio. Without regular review, subscriptions accumulate, unused tools continue to auto-renew, and value assessments are never updated. **→ ***Schedule an annual vendor review — ideally timed before budget season. Walk through this register together: confirm renewals, cancel unused tools, and update cost and ownership fields. A 90-minute joint IT/Business Office session is sufficient for most schools.* |
| --- |

| **[LOW]  ****Contract signing authority informal — not documented** *Vendor Governance  ·  Schedule this year  ·  Quick (½ day)  ·  Head of School / Business Manager* Signing authority is informally understood but not written down. This creates risk during staff transitions. **→ ***Write down the signing authority policy — even a one-paragraph email to relevant staff is a starting point. Formalise it in the staff handbook or IT policy document.* |
| --- |

**Action Plan**

All findings grouped by timing bucket. Assign a named owner to each action before the next renewal cycle.

**Immediate — Do within 30 days**

**[CRITICAL]  ****No Data Processing Agreement in place***  (Seesaw)*

*→ Request the vendor's DPA template immediately. Most EdTech vendors have a standard DPA — if they do not, this is itself a red flag. Sign the DPA before the next renewal and store it in the register.  *[Medium (3 days)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[CRITICAL]  ****No Data Processing Agreement in place***  (Kami)*

*→ Request the vendor's DPA template immediately. Most EdTech vendors have a standard DPA — if they do not, this is itself a red flag. Sign the DPA before the next renewal and store it in the register.  *[Medium (3 days)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[HIGH]  ****Renewal date not known***  (Seesaw)*

*→ Contact the vendor or review the original contract to find the renewal date. Record it in the register and set a calendar reminder at least 60 days in advance.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[HIGH]  ****Admin credentials not documented***  (Seesaw)*

*→ Add the admin credentials for this vendor to the school's shared password manager. Verify at least two people have access.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director]

**[HIGH]  ****FERPA/COPPA compliance not reviewed***  (Seesaw)*

*→ Request the vendor's privacy policy, Student Data Privacy Agreement template, and any SOC 2 or FERPA compliance documentation. Review it and document the outcome before the next renewal.  *[Medium (3 days)  ·  IT Director / Head of School]

**[HIGH]  ****Auto-renewing contract with no tracked reminder***  (Panorama Education)*

*→ Set a calendar reminder at least 60 days before the renewal date — or 30 days before the required cancellation notice deadline if shorter. Assign a named owner to act on the reminder.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[HIGH]  ****Admin credentials not documented***  (Panorama Education)*

*→ Add the admin credentials for this vendor to the school's shared password manager. Verify at least two people have access.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director]

**[HIGH]  ****FERPA/COPPA compliance not reviewed***  (Panorama Education)*

*→ Request the vendor's privacy policy, Student Data Privacy Agreement template, and any SOC 2 or FERPA compliance documentation. Review it and document the outcome before the next renewal.  *[Medium (3 days)  ·  IT Director / Head of School]

**[HIGH]  ****Auto-renewing contract with no tracked reminder***  (Adobe Creative Cloud)*

*→ Set a calendar reminder at least 60 days before the renewal date — or 30 days before the required cancellation notice deadline if shorter. Assign a named owner to act on the reminder.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[HIGH]  ****Auto-renewing contract with no tracked reminder***  (Zoom Pro)*

*→ Set a calendar reminder at least 60 days before the renewal date — or 30 days before the required cancellation notice deadline if shorter. Assign a named owner to act on the reminder.  *[Quick (½ day)  ·  IT Director / Business Office]

**[HIGH]  ****Offboarding does not cover vendor account ownership**

*→ Add vendor account transfer to the IT offboarding checklist. For each departing staff member who owned vendor accounts, reassign those accounts before their last day. Check billing contacts and support portal accounts specifically — these are the most commonly overlooked.  *[Medium (3 days)  ·  HR / IT Director]

**Near-Term — Do within 90 days**

**[HIGH]  ****No signed contract on file***  (Seesaw)*

