**Section VR2 — School-Wide Vendor Governance**

| **Question ID** | **Question** | **Answer** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| VR2.1 | Software approval process | Informal — IT or business office is usually consulted but not required |
| VR2.2 | Contract signing authority | Informal — generally understood but not written down |
| VR2.3 | Spend threshold policy | No — no spend threshold policy |
| VR2.4 | Master vendor register existed before this audit? | Partial — IT has a list and Business Office has a list, but they are separate |
| VR2.5 | Centralized password manager for vendor accounts? | Partial — used for some accounts but not all |
| VR2.6 | Renewal tracking shared between IT and Business Office? | Partial — one party tracks renewals and notifies the other informally |
| VR2.7 | Vendor account offboarding covered? | No — vendor account ownership is not addressed in offboarding |
| VR2.8 | DPAs centrally tracked? | Partial — some DPAs tracked but not all vendors covered |
| VR2.9 | Annual vendor review conducted? | No — no annual review |
| VR2.10 | Biggest unresolved vendor concern | The Veracross situation keeps me up at night — we cannot find the original contract, we do not know what data rights the vendor has, and the renewal is in August. But the broader concern is that we discovered two vendors today (Adobe CC, Zoom Pro) that are auto-renewing on cards nobody is watching, and two more (Seesaw, Panorama) that hold student data without a DPA. This register is the first time all of this has been in one place. The real fix is a formal approval process for new tools and an annual review — right now we are just reacting. |